Well, in fact there _is_ a law against competitors to the PS. Private
letter carrying is _banned_, period.

Packages and "overnight letters" are allowed--though I'm sure the PS
regrets this oversight--but these are priced high. 

(An interesting question: FedEx, for example, ships overnight
enveloped for around $10. And "Second Day Air" for even less. Under
what laws exactly would they be stopped if they offered a further cut
to sending small envelopes for, say, 29 cents?)

