cardboard box to the same address? Duh!

If it's just one letter in a box, this may slide through, but the cost
is high. (Like I said, I don't know the precise statutory language.)

And in fact the laws clearly prohibit including letters in packages,
and the shippers pay lip service to this notion. Enforcement is nearly
impossible, of course. Such a service could not be formally advertised
and run using this scheme.

